        "title": "国会议员简历底稿（2026年6月整理，仓库归档）",
        "published_at": "2026-06-13",
        "checked_at": "2026-10-22",
        "excerpt": "布莱恩·马斯特，男，1980年7月生，密歇根州大急流城市人，大学学历，文学学士学位，2012年6月参加工作，2016年8月加入美国共和党。",
        "tier": 3
      },
      {
        "id": "cdir1",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/app/details/CDIR-2026-02-20",
        "title": "Official Congressional Directory, 119th Congress（2026年2月20日版，美国政府出版局）",
        "published_at": "2026-02-20",
        "checked_at": "2026-11-09",
        "excerpt": "BRIAN J. MAST, Republican, of Fort Pierce, FL; born in Grand Rapids, MI, July 10, 1980; education: B.L.A., economics (concentration), government and environmental studies (minor), Harvard Extension School, Cambridge, MA, 2016; military service: enlisted, U.S. Army, 2000-11 (retired with the rank of Staff Sergeant); professional history: analyst, NA-42 Office of Emergency Response, National Nuclear Security Administration, Department of Energy, 2011-12; instructor, Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, and Firearms; explosive specialist, Department of Homeland Security; election history: elected to the 18th District for the 115th Congress on November 8, 2016; reelected to each succeeding Congress; elected to the 21st District for the 118th Congress on November 8, 2022; reelected to the 119th Congress on November 5, 2024.",
        "tier": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Mast",
        "title": "维基百科：Brian Mast",
        "published_at": null,
        "checked_at": "2026-11-09",
        "excerpt": "In 2016, he obtained a Bachelor of Liberal Arts from the Harvard Extension School with a concentration in economics ... After graduating from high school, Mast enlisted in the United States Army Reserve in May 2000 and became a combat engineer assigned to the 841st Combat Engineer Battalion. In 2006, he transitioned to the active U.S. Army and became an explosive ordnance disposal technician. ... Mast provided explosive and counter-terrorism expertise to the Office of Emergency Operations at the National Nuclear Security Administration from July 2011 to February 2012 ... Constituency: 18th district (2017–2023), 21st district (2023–present); Chair of the House Foreign Affairs Committee, assumed office January 3, 2025",
        "tier": 3
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "url": "https://mast.house.gov/about-brian/",
        "title": "布莱恩·马斯特众议员官网：About Brian",
        "published_at": null,
        "checked_at": "2026-11-09",
        "excerpt": "Congressman Brian Mast is in his fifth term representing the 21st Congressional District of Florida. Prior to his election to Congress, Brian followed in his father’s footsteps by serving in the U.S. Army for more than 12 years ... After his retirement from the Army, he continued working in counter-terrorism and national defense as an Explosive Specialist with the Department of Homeland Security. ... The Transportation and Infrastructure Committee ... The Foreign Affairs Committee, where he serves as Chairman",
        "tier": 1
      }
    ],
